{"step_index":2423,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T11:55:56Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T14:55:56+03:00\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T14:55:56+03:00\nFile Path: `file:///d:/AI_Engineer/Pharmacy-agy/src/fast_match/coordinator.py`\nTotal Lines: 273\nTotal Bytes: 11654\nShowing lines 1 to 60\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: import json\n2: import time\n3: import re\n4: import concurrent.futures\n5: import requests as http_requests\n6: \n7: from ..config import Config\n8: from .search import FastCandidateFinder\n9: from ..match.text_match import normalize_text\n10: \n11: \n12: SYSTEM_PROMPT = \"\"\"You are a pharmaceutical matching assistant.\n13: You will receive a list of cases. Each case has a requested drug name and a list of specific candidate items found in the warehouse.\n14: \n15: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this exact schema:\n16: {\n17:   \"results\": [\n18:     {\n19:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\n20:       \"status\": \"match or no_match or review\",\n21:       \"item_id\": \"string\"\n22:     }\n23:   ]\n24: }\n25: \n26: Rules:\n27: 1. \"match\" means the exact same product, strength, dosage form, and pack size. Set \"item_id\" to the ID of the matching candidate.\n28: 2. \"no_match\" means NONE of the provided candidates are a safe match. Set \"item_id\" to \"\".\n29: 3. \"review\" means there is a plausible candidate but details are ambiguous. Set \"item_id\" to that candidate's ID.\n30: 4. ONLY return results for the cases provided.\n31: 5. DO NOT return markdown blocks. Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\n32: \"\"\"\n33: \n34: class FastCoordinator:\n35:     def __init__(self, config: Config):\n36:         self.config = config\n37: \n38:     def process(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> dict:\n39:         unique_shortages = {}\n40:         for item in shortage_items:\n41:             name = item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")\n42:             if name and name not in unique_shortages:\n43:                 unique_shortages[name] = item\n44:                 \n45:         deduped_shortages = list(unique_shortages.values())\n46: \n47:         print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n48:         print(f\"[FAST ENGINE] Starting Match: {len(shortage_items)} raw -> {len(deduped_shortages)} UNIQUE shortages x {len(warehouse_data)} warehouses\")\n49:         print(f\"{'='*60}\\n\")\n50: \n51:         all_warehouse_results = {}\n52:         found_in = {}\n53: \n54:         for wh_name, wh_items in warehouse_data.items():\n55:             print(f\"\\n{'-'*40}\")\n56:             print(f\"[Warehouse] {wh_name} ({len(wh_items)} items)\")\n57:             print(f\"{'-'*40}\")\n58: \n59:             wh_result = self._match_warehouse(deduped_shortages, wh_items, wh_name)\n60:             all_warehouse_results[wh_name] = wh_result\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
